Track 1: Cicadas Overbias the Food Court
- Story & Context: It started the rainy Tuesday Orville Vance jammed an electrified 1952 dobro pickup into the sound card of an abandoned Galaxian cabinet inside Aladdin’s Castle, filling the empty concourse with the pungent stink of melting phenolic resin. Instead of shorting out, the cabinet began to bellow an unbreakable forty-minute drone in open G, its green monitor flickering violently as thousands of cicadas dropped through the fractured skylight to batter the warm chassis. Frightened security never came, leaving Orville to sink against the damp plywood marquee and rest his forehead on the vibrating coin door. Through the crackling cabinet speaker he crooned an old mountain hymn until his throat went dry, singing "The copper wire is humming like an August afternoon," while the arcade transformer settled into a permanent, sun-drenched thrum.
